# What stays OUT of git — everything derived:
#   data/   — regenerable build data: data/<env>/<area>/cache (tokenized *.tsv)
#             and data/<env>/<area>/reports (generated *.rpt). Safe to delete
#             wholesale; parse.sh + the report scripts rebuild it from input/.
# input/ is committed IN FULL in this DEVELOP repo — the sample CSVs included:
# the whole estate is synthetic (bin/sample/generate.sh) and small, so a fresh
# clone builds the complete site. (The RUNTIME repo keeps its own .gitignore
# with the *.csv rule — its real exports are bulk and never pushed.)
# The rendered docs/ site is committed.
data/

# bin/build.sh's per-run artifacts: the HTML build report (index.html) and the
# raw per-step logs it embeds. Local only, rewritten every run, safe to delete.
# LEADING SLASH: anchored to the repo root on purpose. A bare "build/" also
# matches bin/build/ — the tracked step scripts only bin/build.sh invokes — so a
# NEW script added there would be silently ignored instead of committed.
/build/

# Local archives (e.g. a zipped-up docs/ for sharing) — never part of the build.
*.zip
*.7z

# Finder metadata. Also in most machines' global excludes, but carried here so
# a clone without one stays clean too.
.DS_Store
